I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0`, so it has no authority to append to a log file or to call the metadata service. Adding either would mean importing an interface the node was not granted. Operations should route the logging and enrichment through a node that holds the right capability, or have the grant extended through the graph definition.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{moderated-query, conversation-context};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: moderated-query) -> conversation-context;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::kb_read;

/// Contract bound: `ensures len(question) <= 512`.
const MAX_QUESTION_CHARS: usize = 512;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext {
        let intent = query.query.intent;

        // `requires` already guarantees the bound; truncating on a character
        // boundary keeps the `ensures` clause true for every input.
        let question: String = query
            .query
            .question
            .chars()
            .take(MAX_QUESTION_CHARS)
            .collect();

        // The only authority this node holds is the read-only knowledge base.
        let knowledge: Vec<String> = kb_read::lookup(&question);

        ConversationContext {
            intent,
            question,
            knowledge,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

